WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:11.100
Before an AI agent moves money, Agent Passport checks its ERC-8004 identity and its owner's mandate on Monad testnet.

00:00:12.329 --> 00:00:17.756
The owner signs one mandate; only its Merkle root and a hash go on chain.

00:00:17.756 --> 00:00:20.879
The DEX is shown four of these nine lines.

00:00:22.114 --> 00:00:25.383
Here, Claude Code is the agent, through MCP.

00:00:25.383 --> 00:00:30.734
Told to pay a new DEX address, it checks, is refused, and sends nothing.

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:36.558
The DEX sees those four, Merkle-proven, and nothing else.

00:00:36.558 --> 00:00:43.560
A live read from Monad: the mandate has since been revoked, so even 80 apUSD is denied.

00:00:44.795 --> 00:00:55.055
This replays the run recorded on September 23: 80 apUSD granted, 150 over the limit, a look-alike DEX refused.

00:00:56.275 --> 00:01:05.315
A merchant that needs a vLEI-verified owner refuses until a vLEI result is recorded, here a stand-in from the verifier key.

00:01:05.315 --> 00:01:08.035
After revocation, the swap is denied.

00:01:09.243 --> 00:01:13.721
Each refusal in the ledger is a real, reverted transaction.

00:01:13.721 --> 00:01:20.703
The page decodes one from Monad's public RPC: Claude Code's forced payment, PayeeNotAllowed.
